# LF in the repository, whatever a checkout smudges it to.
#
# The first three were here because a CRLF .py or .tf makes Terraform plan a
# resource as changed on every run, for ever. The next three are the same
# defect in the front end: vite hashes an asset by its bytes, a line ending
# is a byte, and a build from a CRLF source emits a differently-named asset
# for a file nobody edited. DRIFT-01 records both.

*.tf text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf
*.svg text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
